    },
    {
      "claim": "Even for the P-gp substrate sorafenib, oral administration to Abcb1a/1b-/- and Abcg2-/- mice showed no difference in systemic exposure versus wild type, indicating intestinal ABCB1 and ABCG2 do not play a major role in its oral bioavailability; sorafenib was also classified as highly permeable.",
      "card_ids": ["C235", "C212", "C237", "C229"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Low-solubility records for regorafenib, tranilast, nitazoxanide, and other lipophilic compounds do not provide an affirmative threshold-relevant low-F outcome for the query; low solubility alone does not establish F < 20%.",
